   "tag": "div",
   "class": "ins cleared mol-factbox-body",
   "landmarks": [],
   "textLength": 532,
   "text": "Gaslighting involves tricking someone into questioning something they know to be true.\nThe phrase can be traced to the 1938 stage thriller Gas Light, by British author Patrick Hamilton, which was adapted into the 1944 film Gaslight starring Ingrid Bergman as a woman whose controlling husband makes trips into the attic to search for hidden jewellery, igniting a gaslight and causing lights elsewhere",
